# Dropdown option order

Copy this file into the next project's `.cursor/rules/` as-is.

## Master data — always A–Z

Lists of named records (families, items, suppliers, branches, people, units, VAT **labels**, and similar pickers) must appear **A at the top, Z at the bottom**, sorted by the **text the user sees**, not by id, pk, insert order, or enum declaration order.

- Pin empty sentinels first (`All…`, `Choose…`, `—`). Then sort the rest.
- Use locale-aware compare (`localeCompare` with `{ sensitivity: "base", numeric: true }`, or the UI language’s collation). Translated labels must sort in the **current language**.
- Prefer one shared filler (`fillSelect` or equivalent) over per-page option loops. A CSS class cannot sort `<option>`s; SQL `ORDER BY name` is a safety net, not enough when labels are composed or i18n’d.
- Do **not** change table/pagination default order just to fix a picker. Sort at fill time (and/or via an optional `sortValue` when the visible label is a poor key, e.g. `#12 — Supplier`).

```javascript
// BAD — API id order
items.forEach((item) => select.appendChild(option(item.id, item.label)));

// GOOD — placeholder first, then visible label
fillSelect(select, items.map((item) => ({
  value: String(item.id),
  label: `${item.code} — ${item.description}`,
})), "Choose…");
```

Stability over skipping the sort. New dropdowns must use the shared helper so they cannot “forget” to sort.

## Workflow lists — do not alphabetize

Keep author order for closed vocabularies: status/lifecycle, time periods, language, tags, bulk actions, close reasons. Example: Draft → Submitted → Approved, not Approved → Draft.

## This repository

Helper: [`products/static/products/js/select_fill.js`](products/static/products/js/select_fill.js) (`window.fillSelect`). Include it **before** the page script and bump `?v=` (and the branch Service Worker precache when the page is PWA-cached).
